{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — Featured collection
  Phase 6. One section, used for every collection row on the home page.

  The Phase 6 brief offered a second file, sections/best-sellers.liquid. It is
  not here on purpose: Best Sellers and New Drop differ only in which
  collection is selected and what the copy says, and duplicating the Liquid
  would mean fixing every future bug twice. The section ships two presets
  instead — "New Drop" and "Best Sellers" — so both are one click away in the
  Theme Editor with the right defaults already set.

  Sources of truth:
  - PHASE-2-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md sections 9.3 (grid), 13 (card), 27 (commerce),
    29.3 (this section's worked schema).
  - PHASE-1-WEBSITE-AUDIT.md for the eleven issues assigned to this phase.
  - PHASE-5-HERO.md section 16 for what this section inherited.

  SHOPIFY IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH. There is no product data in this file, no
  price string, no ranking logic and no assumption that any collection exists.
  "Best Sellers" names a collection the merchant chooses; this section never
  decides what sells.

  ZERO JavaScript.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign collection = section.settings.collection
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | strip
  assign eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow | strip
  assign description = section.settings.description | strip

  assign cols_d = section.settings.columns_desktop
  assign cols_t = section.settings.columns_tablet
  assign cols_m = section.settings.columns_mobile

  assign surface_class = 'surface-light'
  if section.settings.surface == 'dark'
    assign surface_class = 'surface-dark'
  endif

  assign has_products = false
  if collection != blank and collection.products.size > 0
    assign has_products = true
  endif

  comment
    View all. The destination is the selected collection's own URL. A url
    setting cannot default to a dynamic value, so the override is offered and
    falls back rather than the other way round. No collection URL is ever
    built by hand — Phase 1 NAV-03 recorded six href="#" anchors and this
    phase does not add a seventh.
  endcomment
  assign view_all_url = section.settings.view_all_url
  if view_all_url == blank and collection != blank
    assign view_all_url = collection.url
  endif
  assign view_all_label = section.settings.view_all_label | strip
  assign show_view_all = false
  if section.settings.show_view_all and view_all_url != blank and view_all_label != blank
    assign show_view_all = true
  endif

  comment
    The sizes attribute.

    The section knows the grid, so the section computes this; the card takes it
    as a parameter rather than guessing. Two things make it more than a
    division.

    First, the grid's column count is a CEILING. .product-grid floors every
    track at --product-col-min 272px, so where a viewport cannot carry the
    requested count the grid drops a column and the survivors stretch. Dividing
    by the requested count would then declare a slot narrower than the tile
    actually painted, and the browser would fetch a candidate it has to upscale.
    Measured before this was fixed: at 1024 the New Drop grid painted two 292px
    tracks against a declared 196px.

    Between a tier's minimum width and the width at which the requested count
    first fits, the rendered count is exactly one lower. That threshold is
    computable here, so each tier emits two clauses: the requested count from
    the threshold up, and one fewer below it. Both are exact at every width in
    their range, so nothing is over-declared either.

    Second, the copy-column layout puts the grid in the 2.4 track of
    --split-30-70, which is 72.7% of the row once the 32px split gap is taken
    off. Gutters come from the Phase 2 ladder: 24, 32 and 48 per side.
  endcomment

  assign gap = 32
  comment
    The column gap is not the same at every tier. Below --bp-md the grid
    tightens to --space-4 16px, because a 32px gap between two 147px cards sat
    inside a 24px gutter and read as two bands rather than one row. A narrower
    gap makes the cards WIDER, so the mobile clauses of the sizes attribute
    have to be computed against it or they under-declare the slot.
  endcomment
  assign gap_m = 16
  assign col_min = 272

  comment
    Per-tier row width available to the grid, expressed as the fixed pixels to
    subtract from the viewport. Desktop also loses the copy rail.
  endcomment
  assign chrome_m = 48
  assign chrome_t = 64
  assign chrome_d = 96
  if section.settings.layout == 'with-copy-column'
    assign chrome_d = 128
  endif

  comment
    The viewport at which cols_d first fits. Needed row is
    cols_d * 272 + (cols_d - 1) * 32; for the copy-column layout the grid is
    only 72.7% of the row, so the viewport has to be correspondingly wider.
    1000 / 727 is used rather than a float because Liquid's divided_by on two
    integers truncates, and truncating downward here would put the threshold
    below the width that actually fits.
  endcomment
  assign need_d = cols_d | times: col_min
  assign need_d = cols_d | minus: 1 | times: gap | plus: need_d
  if section.settings.layout == 'with-copy-column'
    assign need_d = need_d | times: 1000 | divided_by: 727 | plus: 1
  endif
  assign threshold_d = need_d | plus: chrome_d

  comment
    Floored at the tier boundary. The desktop column count only takes effect at
    --bp-lg 1024, but the threshold is derived from the column arithmetic alone,
    so the full-bleed layout at three columns computes 976. Left there, the
    clause would match from 976 up while the grid between 976 and 1023 is still
    painting the TABLET count — declaring a slot narrower than the one that
    paints. A sizes clause must never claim a width before the layout that
    produces it applies.

    This section is not consolidated into snippets/grid-sizes.liquid because its
    copy-column layout scales the needed row by 1000/727 above: its derivation
    is genuinely different, not duplicated.
  endcomment
  if threshold_d < 1024
    assign threshold_d = 1024
  endif

  comment
    Below the threshold the grid paints one column fewer, floored at one.
  endcomment
  assign cols_d_low = cols_d | minus: 1
  if cols_d_low < 1
    assign cols_d_low = 1
  endif
  assign cols_t_low = cols_t | minus: 1
  if cols_t_low < 1
    assign cols_t_low = 1
  endif

  comment
    Tablet: does cols_t fit at 768, the tier's own minimum? If not, the tier
    never reaches it, because the next tier starts at 1024.
  endcomment
  assign need_t = cols_t | times: col_min
  assign need_t = cols_t | minus: 1 | times: gap | plus: need_t
  assign row_t_min = 768 | minus: chrome_t
  assign cols_t_used = cols_t
  if need_t > row_t_min
    assign cols_t_used = cols_t_low
  endif

  comment
    Mobile: the floor is 8rem/128px below 768 and the gap is 16px, so the step
    is 144.
  endcomment
  assign need_m = cols_m | times: 128
  assign need_m = cols_m | minus: 1 | times: gap_m | plus: need_m
  assign threshold_m = need_m | plus: chrome_m
  assign cols_m_low = cols_m | minus: 1
  if cols_m_low < 1
    assign cols_m_low = 1
  endif

  assign gaps_d = cols_d | minus: 1 | times: gap
  assign gaps_d_low = cols_d_low | minus: 1 | times: gap
  assign gaps_t = cols_t_used | minus: 1 | times: gap
  assign gaps_m = cols_m | minus: 1 | times: gap_m
  assign gaps_m_low = cols_m_low | minus: 1 | times: gap_m
  assign container = settings.container_width | default: 1440

  comment
    Above the container cap the row stops growing, so the first clause is a
    fixed pixel value rather than a vw expression.
  endcomment
  assign capped_row = container | minus: chrome_d
  if section.settings.layout == 'with-copy-column'
    assign capped_row = capped_row | times: 727 | divided_by: 1000
  endif
  comment
    Integer division truncates, so the cap would be declared one pixel under
    the rendered track — measured 296 against 297 at 1440. One pixel changes
    no candidate, but under-declaring is the direction that costs quality.
  endcomment
  comment
    Divide by what FITS, not by what was asked for. The grid is auto-fill with a
    272px floor, so at the container cap it paints only as many columns as that
    floor allows: with four columns and the container at its 1200px minimum,
    dividing by the requested four declares 253px for a track that actually
    paints 346px — a 27% under-declaration, which makes the browser fetch a
    candidate it then has to upscale.
  endcomment
  assign col_slot = col_min | plus: gap
  assign fits_d = capped_row | plus: gap | divided_by: col_slot
  if fits_d < 1
    assign fits_d = 1
  endif
  assign cols_capped = cols_d
  if fits_d < cols_d
    assign cols_capped = fits_d
  endif
  assign gaps_capped = cols_capped | minus: 1 | times: gap
  assign capped_track = capped_row | minus: gaps_capped | divided_by: cols_capped | plus: 1

  capture sizes_attr
    echo '(min-width: '
    echo container
    echo 'px) '
    echo capped_track
    echo 'px'

    echo ', (min-width: '
    echo threshold_d
    echo 'px) calc(('
    if section.settings.layout == 'with-copy-column'
      echo '(100vw - '
      echo chrome_d
      echo 'px) * 0.727 - '
    else
      echo '100vw - '
      echo chrome_d
      echo 'px - '
    endif
    echo gaps_d
    echo 'px) / '
    echo cols_d
    echo ')'

    echo ', (min-width: 1024px) calc(('
    if section.settings.layout == 'with-copy-column'
      echo '(100vw - '
      echo chrome_d
      echo 'px) * 0.727 - '
    else
      echo '100vw - '
      echo chrome_d
      echo 'px - '
    endif
    echo gaps_d_low
    echo 'px) / '
    echo cols_d_low
    echo ')'

    echo ', (min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - '
    echo chrome_t
    echo 'px - '
    echo gaps_t
    echo 'px) / '
    echo cols_t_used
    echo ')'

    echo ', (min-width: '
    echo threshold_m
    echo 'px) calc((100vw - '
    echo chrome_m
    echo 'px - '
    echo gaps_m
    echo 'px) / '
    echo cols_m
    echo ')'

    echo ', calc((100vw - '
    echo chrome_m
    echo 'px - '
    echo gaps_m_low
    echo 'px) / '
    echo cols_m_low
    echo ')'
  endcapture

  comment
    The card titles sit one level below this section's heading — but the
    heading is a free-text setting a merchant can clear, and when it is blank
    no h2 renders. Hard-coding level 3 would then jump from the hero's h1
    straight to h3, which is the outline defect Phase 1 HTML-03 assigns to this
    phase. The level follows the heading instead.
  endcomment
  assign card_heading_level = 3
  if heading == blank
    assign card_heading_level = 2
  endif

  assign classes = 'featured-collection '
  assign classes = classes | append: surface_class
  assign classes = classes | append: ' featured-collection--' | append: section.settings.layout
  assign classes = classes | append: ' featured-collection--pt-' | append: section.settings.spacing_top
  assign classes = classes | append: ' featured-collection--pb-' | append: section.settings.spacing_bottom
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Nothing is rendered on the live storefront until there are products to show.
  The test is has_products, not "is a collection chosen": a merchant can point
  the section at a collection and later empty or unpublish it, and the result
  would otherwise be a full-height band of copy and a View all button over
  nothing — the very thing a heading floating above an empty band describes.

  In the Theme Editor the section always renders, with a note saying which of
  the two is missing, so the merchant can see and configure it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if has_products == false and request.design_mode == false -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Not configured yet: render nothing, and request nothing. The stylesheets
    are emitted inside this branch rather than at the top of the file so an
    unconfigured section costs no requests either.
  {%- endcomment -%}
{%- else -%}

{{ 'component-product-card.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'section-featured-collection.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  The column counts are merchant settings, so they arrive as scoped custom
  properties rather than as inline style on the grid: an inline declaration
  would outrank every media query and pin the mobile count to all three tiers.
  The section id scopes them, which is what lets two instances of this section
  on one page carry different counts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% style %}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-grid { --product-cols: {{ cols_m }}; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-grid { --product-cols: {{ cols_t }}; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .product-grid { --product-cols: {{ cols_d }}; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div
  class="{{ classes }}"
  {% if section.settings.anchor_id != blank %}id="{{ section.settings.anchor_id | handle }}"{% endif %}
>
  <div class="featured-collection__inner container">
    <div class="featured-collection__copy">
      {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="featured-collection__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          An h2, never an h1. Phase 5 established the home page's single h1 in
          the hero and Phase 1 HTML-03 recorded the outline as the defect this
          fixes.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h2 class="featured-collection__heading">{{ heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if description != blank -%}
        <p class="featured-collection__description">{{ description }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if show_view_all -%}
        <a class="featured-collection__cta button button--primary" href="{{ view_all_url }}">
          {{ view_all_label }}
          {% render 'icon-arrow' %}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="featured-collection__products">
      {%- if has_products -%}
        <ul class="product-grid" role="list">
          {%- for product in collection.products limit: section.settings.products_to_show -%}
            <li class="product-grid__item">
              {% render 'product-card',
                product: product,
                heading_level: card_heading_level,
                sizes: sizes_attr,
                show_price: section.settings.show_price,
                show_compare_at: section.settings.show_compare_at_price,
                show_swatches: section.settings.show_swatches
              %}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
        <p class="featured-collection__notice">
          {%- if collection == blank -%}
            {{ 'sections.featured_collection.no_collection' | t }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ 'sections.featured_collection.empty_collection' | t }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection row",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "featured-collection-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Collection"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "Collection",
      "info": "Products, prices, images and availability all come from this collection. Nothing is set in the theme. Until a collection is chosen the section does not render on the live store."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "products_to_show",
      "label": "Products to show",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3,
      "info": "A count that divides evenly into the column count fills its rows. Three products in a two-column grid leaves one on a row of its own."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "New Drop /"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "The Faithful",
      "info": "Renders as a level-2 heading. The page's only level-1 heading belongs to the hero."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Description",
      "default": "Premium Essentials for a Higher Purpose."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "View all"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_view_all",
      "label": "Show the view all button",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "view_all_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "View All Products"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "view_all_url",
      "label": "Button link",
      "info": "Leave empty and the button points at the collection chosen above. Set it only to send people somewhere else."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "surface",
      "label": "Colour scheme",
      "info": "The theme switches text, border, accent and focus colours to suit the band. Muted gold is a dark-surface accent; on cream a darker gold is substituted automatically.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "light",
          "label": "Cream"
        },
        {
          "value": "dark",
          "label": "Ink"
        }
      ],
      "default": "light"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "Layout",
      "info": "The copy column takes about a third of the row, so the grid beside it carries fewer products per row: a three-column grid reaches three columns at 1440px wide with the copy beside it, and at 1024px with the copy above it.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "with-copy-column",
          "label": "Copy beside the products"
        },
        {
          "value": "full-width",
          "label": "Copy above the products"
        }
      ],
      "default": "with-copy-column"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Grid"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "These are maximums. A tile never drops below a readable width, so if a viewport cannot carry the count you choose, the grid drops a column rather than squeezing one."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "label": "Columns, desktop",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_tablet",
      "label": "Columns, tablet",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 3,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_mobile",
      "label": "Columns, mobile",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 3,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Product card"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_price",
      "label": "Show price",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_compare_at_price",
      "label": "Show the original price when a product is reduced",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Shown beside the current price, struck through and muted. There is no sale badge: the two prices are the signal."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_swatches",
      "label": "Show colourway swatches",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Only appears where a product has more than one colour and swatches are configured on that option in Shopify admin. Colours are never guessed from a product's images."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_top",
      "label": "Space above",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "None"
        },
        {
          "value": "tight",
          "label": "Tight"
        },
        {
          "value": "standard",
          "label": "Standard"
        }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_bottom",
      "label": "Space below",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "None"
        },
        {
          "value": "tight",
          "label": "Tight"
        },
        {
          "value": "standard",
          "label": "Standard"
        }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor_id",
      "label": "Anchor",
      "info": "Optional. Lets a menu item or a button link to this section, for example shop."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "New Drop",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "New Drop /",
        "heading": "The Faithful",
        "description": "Premium Essentials for a Higher Purpose.",
        "view_all_label": "View All Products",
        "surface": "light",
        "layout": "with-copy-column",
        "products_to_show": 3,
        "columns_desktop": 3,
        "columns_tablet": 2,
        "columns_mobile": 2,
        "spacing_top": "standard",
        "spacing_bottom": "standard",
        "anchor_id": "shop"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Best Sellers",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Best Sellers /",
        "heading": "The Pieces That Define The Movement",
        "description": "Chosen by the community.",
        "view_all_label": "Shop All Best Sellers",
        "surface": "dark",
        "layout": "full-width",
        "products_to_show": 4,
        "columns_desktop": 4,
        "columns_tablet": 2,
        "columns_mobile": 2,
        "spacing_top": "standard",
        "spacing_bottom": "standard"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
